-- Federal-State Extended Unemployment Compensation Act of 1970 (Pub. L. 91-373, title II)
-- as the OLRC sets it out in the note under 26 U.S.C. 3304.
-- NOUNS ONLY: the enumerations and records the other euca- modules share. No rules.
--
-- Every module that needs one of these imports this module. A noun is declared once, here, so
-- that two modules written separately cannot invent two records for the same thing.
-- Weeks are carried as the DATE on which the week begins (s 205(11): a week is as the applicable
-- State law defines it). Rates of unemployment are plain percentage points: 5.5 means 5.5 per cent.
-- Amounts of money are plain NUMBERs of dollars.

§ `Nouns of the Federal-State Extended Unemployment Compensation Act of 1970`

§§ `Parties and places (ss 202, 204, 205)`

-- The parties the Act names. The Act never names the individual by a defined term; it says
-- "an individual". Officials appear here only so that a rule can say who decides or who pays.
@ref s 205(7), (8), (9) and s 204(e)
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `the State`
    `the State agency`
    `the Secretary of Labor`
    `the Secretary of the Treasury`
    `the United States`

-- s 205(8): "State" includes the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, and the
-- Virgin Islands. A place the definition does not name is neither included nor excluded by it.
@ref s 205(8)
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `a State of the United States`
    `the District of Columbia`
    `the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico`
    `the Virgin Islands`
    `a place the definition of State does not name`

@ref s 205(8)
DECLARE `Status of a place under the definition of State` IS ONE OF
    `counts as a State for this title`
    `is not named by the definition of State, which says only what a State includes`

§§ `Benefit year, base period and the extended benefit period (ss 202, 203, 205)`

-- s 205(5): the benefit year is as defined in the applicable State law.
@ref s 205(5)
DECLARE `Benefit year` HAS
    `first day of the benefit year` IS A DATE
    `last day of the benefit year`  IS A DATE

-- s 205(6): the base period is as determined under the applicable State law for the benefit year.
@ref s 205(6)
DECLARE `Base period` HAS
    `first day of the base period` IS A DATE
    `last day of the base period`  IS A DATE

-- s 203(a): an extended benefit period runs from one week to another. A period that has not yet
-- ended has no last week.
@ref s 203(a)
DECLARE `Extended benefit period` HAS
    `first week of the extended benefit period` IS A DATE
    `last week of the extended benefit period`  IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `The individual's position on regular compensation (s 202(a)(1))`

@ref s 202(a)(1)
DECLARE `Regular compensation position` HAS
    `received all the regular compensation available on the base period employment or wages` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rights to regular compensation for the week under the State law`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `rights to regular compensation for the week under another State's unemployment compensation law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `compensation for the week under another Federal law`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `receiving compensation for the week under the unemployment compensation law of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The work test (s 202(a)(3))`

-- s 202(a)(3)(A)(i): the Act speaks of an offer of suitable work (the step is to accept it) and of
-- suitable work to which the State agency referred the individual (the step is to apply for it).
-- Only the step that matches how the work reached the individual is read.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(i)
DECLARE `How the work reached the individual` IS ONE OF
    `offered to the individual`
    `referred to the individual by the State agency`

-- One offer of work, or one referral, and every fact the subparagraphs C and D need about it.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(i), (C), (D)
DECLARE `Offer of work or referral` HAS
    `how the work reached the individual` IS A `How the work reached the individual`
    `the individual accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual applied for the work to which the State agency referred them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is within the individual's capabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual furnished evidence satisfactory to the State agency that prospects of work in the customary occupation are good` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicable State law treats the work as suitable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gross average weekly remuneration payable for the position` IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year` IS A NUMBER
    `supplemental unemployment compensation benefits payable to the individual for the week` IS A NUMBER
    `the position was offered to the individual in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the position was listed with the State employment service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `State law, so far as consistent with C and E, would deny compensation for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wages the position pays per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `Fair Labor Standards Act section 6(a)(1) minimum wage per hour, without regard to any exemption` IS A NUMBER
    `highest applicable State or local minimum wage per hour, or 0 if there is none` IS A NUMBER

-- s 202(a)(3)(A)(ii), (E): the individual's effort to find work in the week, and the two
-- exemptions the State may choose to apply.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(ii), (E)
DECLARE `Search for work` HAS
    `engaged in a systematic and sustained effort to obtain work during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided tangible evidence to the State agency of that effort` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before a court of the United States or of a State pursuant to a lawfully issued summons to appear for jury duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalized for treatment of an emergency or a life-threatening condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the jury duty exemption applies to recipients of regular benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State chooses to apply the jury duty exemption to recipients of extended benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hospitalization exemption applies to recipients of regular benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State chooses to apply the hospitalization exemption to recipients of extended benefits` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 202(a)(3)(B): what has happened since an earlier failure under subparagraph A.
-- NOTHING for the week of the failure means that there was no such failure.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(B)
DECLARE `Earlier failure` HAS
    `week in which the failure occurred, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `weeks of employment that began after the failure and before the week claimed` IS A NUMBER
    `remuneration earned for being so employed` IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Disqualifications and the employment requirement (s 202(a)(4), (5))`

@ref s 202(a)(4)
DECLARE `Kind of disqualification` IS ONE OF
    `voluntarily leaving employment`
    `being discharged for misconduct`
    `refusing suitable employment`

@ref s 202(a)(4)
DECLARE Disqualification HAS
    `kind of disqualification` IS A `Kind of disqualification`
    `the State law has terminated the disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the termination is based upon employment subsequent to the date of the disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 202(a)(5)
DECLARE `Employment in the base period` HAS
    `weeks of full-time insured employment in the base period` IS A NUMBER
    `earnings covered by the State law in the base period` IS A NUMBER
    `most recent weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER
    `insured wages in the calendar quarter of the base period in which they were highest` IS A NUMBER
    `the State law uses the 20 weeks of full-time insured employment method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State law uses the earnings above 40 times the weekly benefit amount method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State law uses the earnings above one and a half times the highest quarter method` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 202(a)(5)
DECLARE `Result of the employment requirement` IS ONE OF
    `the individual has the required employment`
    `the individual lacks the required employment`
    `the State law has chosen no method, which section 202(a)(5) requires it to do`

§§ `The extended compensation account and interstate claims (s 202(b), (c))`

@ref s 202(b)(1), (3)
DECLARE `Account facts` HAS
    `total regular compensation payable during the benefit year, including dependents' allowances` IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER
    `regular compensation paid or deemed paid during the benefit year` IS A NUMBER
    `the State law reduces the account by additional compensation paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `additional compensation paid or deemed paid for prior weeks in the benefit year that did not begin in an extended benefit period` IS A NUMBER
    `the week begins in a high unemployment period` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 202(c)(1), (2)
DECLARE `Interstate claim` HAS
    `extended compensation would but for the cessation rule have been payable for the week pursuant to an interstate claim under the interstate benefit payment plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an extended benefit period is in effect for the week in the State where the claim was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier weeks for which extended compensation was payable pursuant to the interstate claim from the account` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Indicators of high unemployment (s 203(d), (e), (f))`

-- s 203(d), (f): the State is "on" or "off" for each week. A reading is the verdict for one week.
-- The two records below hold the figures a verdict rests on; the week they are about is passed
-- beside them, so that the insured unemployment test and the alternative trigger are always
-- applied to the same week.
@ref s 203(a), (d), (f)
DECLARE `Indicator reading` HAS
    `week beginning` IS A DATE
    `State on indicator` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 203(d)(1), (d)(2) and the closing paragraph of (d): the insured unemployment test.
-- NOTHING for the date an option is established means that the State law has not adopted the option.
@ref s 203(d)
DECLARE `Insured unemployment reading` HAS
    `rate of insured unemployment for the week and the preceding twelve weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the first preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the second preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `rate for the corresponding thirteen-week period ending in the third preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `date from which the State law adopts the 6 per cent option` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date from which the State law adopts the three-year comparison option` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- s 203(f): the alternative trigger on the rate of total unemployment.
@ref s 203(f)
DECLARE `Total unemployment reading` HAS
    `average rate of total unemployment (seasonally adjusted) for the most recent 3 months for which data for all States are published` IS A NUMBER
    `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the first preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the second preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `average rate for the corresponding 3-month period ending in the third preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER
    `the State law adopts the alternative trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date from which the State law adopts the three-year comparison option` IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `Payments to States (s 204)`

@ref s 204(a)(1)
DECLARE `Kind of compensation paid` IS ONE OF
    `extended compensation`
    `regular compensation`

@ref s 204(a), (b), (c)
DECLARE `Compensation paid for a week` HAS
    `kind of compensation paid` IS A `Kind of compensation paid`
    `amount paid for the week` IS A NUMBER
    `extended compensation paid to the individual earlier in the benefit year` IS A NUMBER
    `regular compensation paid or deemed paid to the individual for prior weeks in the benefit year` IS A NUMBER
    `the week is in the individual's eligibility period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `smallest of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly benefit amount, including allowances for dependents, for weeks of total unemployment` IS A NUMBER
    `section 202(b)(3)(A) applies to the week` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State is entitled to reimbursement under a Federal law other than this title` IS A BOOLEAN
    `first week in the eligibility period for which extended compensation or sharable regular compensation is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State law provides for payment of regular compensation for a first week of otherwise compensable unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `benefits are not payable for the week by reason of section 233 of the Trade Act of 1974` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount that would be paid for the week if the State rounded down to the nearest lower full dollar` IS A NUMBER
    `base period wages attributable to services to which section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue Code applies` IS A NUMBER
    `total base period wages` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Definitions (s 205)`

@ref s 205(1), (2), (3), (4)
DECLARE `Payment to an individual` HAS
    `cash benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable with respect to the individual's unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable under a State unemployment compensation law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable pursuant to 5 U.S.C. chapter 85` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payable to exhaustees by reason of conditions of high unemployment or by reason of other special factors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for a week of unemployment beginning in an extended benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under provisions of the State law which satisfy the requirements of this title with respect to the payment of extended compensation` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Self-employment assistance (s 208)`

@ref s 208(b)
DECLARE `Paragraph of the section 3306(t) definition` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (3)(B)`
    `paragraph (5)`
